WEBVTT

00:08.420 --> 00:11.780
Mister Jade was so amazing 
in that demo battle yesterday.

00:12.090 --> 00:14.000
I've love to see it again.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.680
There's a rumor that he's been 
visiting Iffole Counter a lot lately.

00:18.680 --> 00:21.200
Really?! I envy them so much!

00:21.870 --> 00:25.650
<i>It's really nothing worth envying.</i>

00:25.650 --> 00:28.670
<i>But more importantly, that birthday vacation!</i>

00:29.300 --> 00:32.650
<i>I should get serious about thinking up
 a way to improve the workflow.</i>

00:41.370 --> 00:43.400
<i>Whoa! Don't you dare!</i>

00:43.400 --> 00:46.840
<i>I swear, if you yell out my name 
in the middle of this lecture...</i>

00:48.350 --> 00:49.150
<i>Huh?</i>

00:53.300 --> 00:56.910
<i>Oh, right. The Image 
Improvement Campaign, was it?</i>

00:57.850 --> 01:01.060
<i>He normally acts so familiar
 that it drives me nuts,</i>

01:01.060 --> 01:03.630
<i>so I don't have to wear my 
business smile around him,</i>

01:03.630 --> 01:05.610
<i>or put up any kind of front,</i>

01:05.610 --> 01:08.460
<i>or even hide my real feelings.</i>

01:08.860 --> 01:11.420
<i>Wait, what am I thinking?!</i>

01:12.410 --> 01:17.050
<i>Why do I have to feel so distressed 
over the likes of him?</i>

01:21.410 --> 01:25.270
<b>Adventurers' Guild, Court of Inquiry</b>

01:21.500 --> 01:25.270
Jade Scrade, we are disappointed in you.

01:25.570 --> 01:29.780
We told you that Silver Sword is only 
Silver Sword when it gives us results.

01:30.220 --> 01:34.890
What we want are adventurers who do 
not sully the name of Silver Sword.

01:34.890 --> 01:37.740
We cannot entrust you lot with that anymore.

01:38.650 --> 01:40.700
Let's give them a bit more time.

01:41.100 --> 01:44.160
Would that not defeat the 
purpose of Silver Sword?

01:44.160 --> 01:46.710
There are many who 
can claim to be strong.

01:47.370 --> 01:51.580
But physical strength alone 
isn't enough to be the best.

01:51.900 --> 01:53.500
Yes, but...

01:53.500 --> 01:56.720
I believe this is the right choice.

02:00.910 --> 02:02.470
<i>I want to have faith.</i>

02:03.100 --> 02:07.120
<i>Just as Glen had faith in us back then.</i>

03:48.410 --> 03:51.500
Ah, it's you, Jade. What's the matter?

03:57.900 --> 04:01.130
The past fifteen years have flown by.

04:01.530 --> 04:07.140
As you know, the Silver Sword of two 
generations ago conquered the Fortress of Ash.

04:07.930 --> 04:12.140
And all of them except me lost their lives.

04:12.640 --> 04:14.860
Including our healer, Lynn Riche...

04:15.730 --> 04:17.650
my daughter.

04:18.120 --> 04:21.150
Today happens to be the 
anniversary of her death.

04:23.150 --> 04:26.630
Lynn taught me something very important.

04:27.440 --> 04:28.910
I'm proud to call her my daughter.

04:30.430 --> 04:33.770
Anyway, did you have business with me?

04:34.170 --> 04:36.330
I... What was it again?

04:36.330 --> 04:40.300
What's this? You're too young 
to be getting forgetful.

04:43.350 --> 04:44.410
Jade...

04:44.890 --> 04:47.970
When that young lady and the 
dark gods fight with their Dia skills,

04:47.970 --> 04:52.610
you hold your own with your Sigurth skills.
Your strength is the real deal.

04:53.560 --> 04:56.850
You will most likely be guildmaster one day.

04:56.850 --> 04:59.950
Learn as much as you can now, 
while you have the time.

05:12.580 --> 05:13.450
Jade.

05:14.510 --> 05:17.370
Did Mister Glen pass by here?

05:17.760 --> 05:21.250
He said he was going out for 
a walk and did not return.

05:22.030 --> 05:24.260
He was here just a moment ago.

05:24.750 --> 05:26.250
You just missed him.

05:26.250 --> 05:27.760
I see.

05:28.330 --> 05:31.760
Hey... Has anything changed with Glen lately?

05:31.760 --> 05:33.310
I cannot answer that.

05:33.990 --> 05:37.370
Oh, okay. Sorry for asking 
a weird question like that.

05:38.130 --> 05:42.480
You suspect that Mister Glen is 
the man in black, do you not?

05:45.690 --> 05:46.990
Mark my words.

05:47.550 --> 05:53.510
Mister Glen is not so foolish 
as to endanger this world.

05:54.810 --> 05:55.490
Yeah.

05:56.760 --> 05:59.790
But he is the kind of man who 
would use his skills to run away

06:00.870 --> 06:05.050
when too much annoying desk 
work starts piling up.

06:07.090 --> 06:10.620
He was not always the 
good-natured man he is today.

06:11.240 --> 06:13.610
He used to be cold, stubborn, and selfish.

06:14.910 --> 06:17.960
Some even said he lacked a human soul.

06:18.650 --> 06:20.430
Really?

06:20.430 --> 06:22.820
And do you know what it was that changed him?

06:23.970 --> 06:25.250
Lynn?

06:25.250 --> 06:29.040
She was an orphan, and 
raising her as his daughter

06:29.040 --> 06:31.320
forced him to mature, as well.

06:31.840 --> 06:34.660
But then he lost her.

06:38.300 --> 06:43.770
I cannot even imagine 
how much Lynn meant to him.

06:44.460 --> 06:47.510
Perhaps, for her sake, he would even...

06:56.890 --> 06:58.980
It's finally over!

06:58.980 --> 07:01.540
It's nice that we don't have to work overtime,

07:01.540 --> 07:04.220
but this training is exhausting in its own way.

07:04.220 --> 07:06.480
You slept through the whole thing, though.

07:06.480 --> 07:08.450
Well, I woke up tired!

07:10.270 --> 07:13.320
I don't know how you stayed awake through that.

07:13.320 --> 07:15.880
There's a trick to it.

07:15.880 --> 07:19.750
No matter how sleepy you are,
 you can't just lie down in front of people.

07:19.750 --> 07:22.810
So what you do is... close one eye at a time!

07:22.810 --> 07:23.500
Huh?

07:23.500 --> 07:25.280
First, you let your right eye rest,

07:25.280 --> 07:27.750
then you let your left eye rest.

07:27.750 --> 07:29.940
If you rest your eyes in turns like that,

07:29.940 --> 07:33.010
you'll be awakened from the 
onslaught of sleepiness!

07:33.450 --> 07:38.430
I don't think I've ever pitied 
you as much as I do right now.

07:38.430 --> 07:39.560
Wait, why?!

07:39.560 --> 07:42.560
Anyway! The cafeteria sure 
was crowded, wasn't it?

07:43.400 --> 07:45.020
Yeah.

07:45.020 --> 07:49.850
I thought we'd be the only ones using it 
so late since we're staying overnight.

07:50.170 --> 07:53.630
They were probably all getting 
ready to go work overtime.

07:53.630 --> 07:56.400
I hope a table opens up soon.

07:59.980 --> 08:02.970
I'll go take another look!

08:03.740 --> 08:04.830
Reckless...

08:06.020 --> 08:07.840
How goes the training?

08:09.060 --> 08:11.670
You work at Iffole Counter, right?

08:12.080 --> 08:13.340
Yes...

08:13.340 --> 08:15.860
Even your voice is cute!

08:15.860 --> 08:20.850
All the receptionists here are pretty, 
but I knew you were the cutest!

08:22.350 --> 08:26.310
It's tough when you're new and 
there's so much you don't know, right?

08:26.570 --> 08:29.020
I'd be glad to teach you some things,

08:29.020 --> 08:31.860
so maybe we can use this chance to get closer.

08:33.600 --> 08:35.610
Please excuse me.

08:35.610 --> 08:37.240
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

08:37.760 --> 08:40.930
Why don't we chat about the things 
that stress us out from day to day?

08:40.930 --> 08:43.250
You're staying at the
 training hall tonight, right?

08:43.250 --> 08:43.970
Let me go!

08:43.970 --> 08:47.750
Is that how you're supposed to treat 
your senior staffer, little newbie?

08:47.750 --> 08:48.710
The hell, man?!

08:48.980 --> 08:50.710
Want to tell me about 
what stresses you out?

08:52.500 --> 08:54.220
M-M-Mister Jade!

08:55.720 --> 09:01.050
Aren't you one of the guys who showed up
 to ogle the receptionists yesterday?

09:02.770 --> 09:05.000
Uh, I...

09:05.000 --> 09:07.190
I can easily find out who you work for.

09:07.530 --> 09:10.770
If they're stressing you out that much, 
I can take it to the top for you.

09:11.130 --> 09:13.220
N-No, really, I appreciate the thought, but...

09:13.750 --> 09:15.740
Well, gotta go!

09:16.820 --> 09:19.620
<i>There are guys like that at the guild, too?</i>

09:20.380 --> 09:24.330
Even if this is guild HQ, you should 
be careful when you're alone.

09:30.060 --> 09:31.490
Um...

09:32.570 --> 09:35.800
Thank you... for helping me.

09:36.800 --> 09:37.460
Sure.

09:41.630 --> 09:42.890
<i>That's it?</i>

09:43.430 --> 09:46.560
<i>Any other time, he wouldn't leave me alone.</i>

09:47.450 --> 09:50.820
<i>Then I'd be able to complain about him.</i>

09:53.100 --> 09:55.070
<i>Oh, darn it!</i>

09:55.580 --> 09:59.450
Your Image Improvement Campaign is 
having the opposite effect, you know.

09:59.950 --> 10:00.820
Huh?!

10:01.160 --> 10:04.040
It throws me off when you act all distant!

10:04.040 --> 10:06.160
I don't see why you can't just act like always!

10:06.660 --> 10:08.670
Y-You... don't mind?

10:08.670 --> 10:09.560
Huh?!

10:10.160 --> 10:12.230
I do, but it's fine!

10:12.230 --> 10:15.050
It's creepy when the guy who's 
usually pestering me nonstop

10:15.050 --> 10:18.680
suddenly starts acting like he's not even there!

10:20.680 --> 10:23.660
S-So... well...

10:24.570 --> 10:27.180
Stop being so curt with me.

10:29.760 --> 10:31.030
Anyway!

10:31.030 --> 10:34.070
Just go back to the way you were! Got it?

10:34.070 --> 10:35.590
G-Got it!

10:36.110 --> 10:36.810
Hmph!

10:37.990 --> 10:41.740
Was I actually... making you feel bad?

10:42.900 --> 10:44.120
Yes.

10:44.690 --> 10:48.050
Sorry. I'm glad you were honest with me.

10:48.360 --> 10:50.690
I'm not good at this kind of thing.

10:50.690 --> 10:54.150
No kidding! You're outrageously bad at it!

10:56.100 --> 10:59.340
But... I don't mind that.

11:03.060 --> 11:05.060
Ms. Alina!

11:05.460 --> 11:07.560
Oh, Mister Jade's here, too?

11:07.560 --> 11:09.380
Where'd that come from?

11:09.380 --> 11:11.710
There still weren't any tables open,

11:11.710 --> 11:14.010
so I gave up and bought this at the shop!

11:14.370 --> 11:16.320
I got some for you, too!

11:16.580 --> 11:18.190
Really? Thanks.

11:18.190 --> 11:21.820
By the way, Mister Jade,
 there's something I wanted to ask you.

11:22.050 --> 11:22.900
What's up?

11:22.900 --> 11:27.740
Have you heard the rumors about the 
reaper that appears in the training hall?

11:27.740 --> 11:30.870
Well, yeah. But they're just rumors, right?

11:30.870 --> 11:31.960
There, you see?

11:32.290 --> 11:35.740
This is the problem with people 
whose sense of fear is broken.

11:35.740 --> 11:37.670
What if it really does show up?

11:38.010 --> 11:39.980
It might be out there in the dark right now,

11:39.980 --> 11:44.750
blending into the darkness with its 
black robe, waiting to take us away.

11:44.750 --> 11:46.560
A black robe?

11:46.820 --> 11:49.570
Yes, that's what I heard.

11:49.900 --> 11:52.960
I see. Let me know if anything happens.

11:52.960 --> 11:54.670
I'll stay at the training hall tonight.

11:54.670 --> 11:57.420
Ooh, that makes me feel a lot better!

11:57.420 --> 11:59.140
Thank you so much!

11:59.140 --> 12:02.070
Hey! They found a new dungeon!

12:02.070 --> 12:04.080
The Civi Cathedral?

12:04.410 --> 12:06.030
Seven floors?!

12:06.270 --> 12:08.370
That's a huge dungeon!

12:08.370 --> 12:12.390
All the reception desks are so overrun,
they're about to blow.

12:12.390 --> 12:15.190
We've gotta get things ready for tomorrow,
or someone's gonna die!

12:15.960 --> 12:18.480
Ms. Alina, did you hear that?

12:19.210 --> 12:21.800
Yes. Every word.

12:22.300 --> 12:23.750
That means...

12:24.060 --> 12:27.390
When training's over,
we're going back to a bloodbath?!

12:27.880 --> 12:29.580
Seven floors, huh?

12:29.580 --> 12:32.050
How long would that take to complete?

12:32.050 --> 12:35.900
But, hey! As long as the training's 
going on, we're safe!

12:35.900 --> 12:37.820
Because we're busy training!

12:37.820 --> 12:40.150
We can forget about the 
outside world while we're—

12:40.150 --> 12:41.400
You two!

12:41.400 --> 12:45.030
You're receptionists from 
Iffole Counter, correct?

12:45.030 --> 12:47.530
Yes, that's correct.

12:47.770 --> 12:49.960
This was delivered for you.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.160
For us?

12:51.770 --> 12:54.170
Unprocessed quest applications.

12:54.490 --> 12:57.970
The counter chief said,
"We'll never get these done in time,"

12:57.970 --> 13:00.170
"so take some of the load for us."

13:00.900 --> 13:01.920
Wha...

13:02.070 --> 13:05.970
What in the hell?!

13:07.000 --> 13:12.350
Why... Why do I have to work 
overtime even during training?!

13:12.350 --> 13:15.810
That piece of shit counter chief!

13:16.140 --> 13:20.520
Please stop releasing an aura 
that's scarier than a ghost's.

13:21.910 --> 13:26.530
Wasn't our safety supposed to 
be guaranteed during training?

13:26.530 --> 13:29.530
My tiny little sliver of peace...

13:29.530 --> 13:30.950
Yeah, but...

13:30.950 --> 13:34.120
it's gonna be even worse later 
if we don't do it all now.

13:34.630 --> 13:35.640
I know that.

13:36.210 --> 13:39.400
Once training is over,
some real carnage awaits us.

13:39.400 --> 13:42.880
We have to take out all this 
unprocessed paperwork today!

13:42.880 --> 13:44.370
Roger that!

13:44.370 --> 13:47.380
But please don't go to sleep before me, okay?

13:49.610 --> 13:50.760
Uh, what's that?

13:51.300 --> 13:55.620
Good luck salt. It'll protect 
me from evil spirits.

13:55.620 --> 13:56.850
Ah, okay...

13:56.850 --> 14:01.220
Seriously, don't go to sleep 
before me, no matter what!

14:01.220 --> 14:02.480
Yeah, sure.

14:06.110 --> 14:07.580
Skill activate!

14:07.580 --> 14:09.490
Sigurth Beast!

14:19.870 --> 14:20.810
Jade!

14:20.810 --> 14:22.040
Don't overwork yourself!

14:22.040 --> 14:23.810
That's enough for now!

14:24.780 --> 14:27.050
I'm fine. Let's keep going.

14:27.280 --> 14:29.630
It's obvious you're at your limit!

14:30.090 --> 14:30.890
Not yet.

14:31.610 --> 14:33.720
I can't get worn out just from...

14:35.930 --> 14:38.960
You're not gonna be of any use 
when we actually need you!

14:40.630 --> 14:43.860
That's true. I'll take a little break.

14:48.480 --> 14:51.380
The reaper in the rumors is the man in black?

14:51.740 --> 14:54.550
You think it'd really be that easy?

14:54.550 --> 14:58.120
Someone let Heitz into the guild.

14:58.120 --> 14:59.540
Which means...

14:59.540 --> 15:04.480
the so-called reaper that's been 
showing up here could be the man in black.

15:04.480 --> 15:06.120
I guess...

15:07.010 --> 15:12.510
Do you guys suspect Glen 
of being the man in black?

15:14.550 --> 15:16.510
But that doesn't make sense!

15:16.510 --> 15:19.390
If he wanted to resurrect a dark god,

15:19.390 --> 15:23.020
he wouldn't let Alina,
someone who can kill dark gods, run free!

15:23.320 --> 15:26.330
I know it sounds like a contradiction, but...

15:26.330 --> 15:29.030
You just can't shake the suspicion, right?

15:31.360 --> 15:33.530
You're both just awful!

15:38.220 --> 15:40.150
I want to trust him, too.

15:40.730 --> 15:43.650
The idea that a guy who values 
life as much as Glen does...

15:45.700 --> 15:48.490
Perhaps, for her sake, he would even...

15:50.270 --> 15:54.200
If we can catch the man in black, 
everything will make sense.

15:57.350 --> 16:00.230
<b>Guild Headquarters, Research Hall</b>

16:04.670 --> 16:08.360
To think these are all 
magical sigils for Dia skills...

16:09.260 --> 16:11.530
It never ceases to blow my mind.

16:12.320 --> 16:17.160
Even after the dark god's 
body died, these remained.

16:17.160 --> 16:20.820
In other words, these could be 
called the dark god's true body.

16:22.270 --> 16:27.710
Why did the ancestors give the Relics 
we call "dark gods" human forms?

16:28.540 --> 16:30.450
I definitely wouldn't have done that.

16:30.970 --> 16:34.050
Creating humans would just 
be a massive headache.

16:38.250 --> 16:40.670
That's it! Of course!

16:40.670 --> 16:46.690
It'd be faster to remake humans 
that already exist into Relics!

16:47.190 --> 16:49.570
Then could this be...

17:08.400 --> 17:09.170
Someone—

17:29.260 --> 17:31.480
Are you kidding me?!

17:31.740 --> 17:34.980
Come on, Ms. Alina! Wake up!

17:35.390 --> 17:36.910
Please, Ms. Alina!

17:37.280 --> 17:40.350
I told you not to go to sleep before me!

17:40.870 --> 17:44.640
P-Please don't leave me all by myself!

17:55.300 --> 17:57.760
Ms. Alina! Ms. Alina, come on!

18:01.380 --> 18:04.390
Wake up! Please wake up!

18:29.580 --> 18:31.380
I hate you.

18:32.540 --> 18:39.680
I hate you... I hate you... 
I hate you... I hate you...

18:39.680 --> 18:42.140
Begone, evil spirit! Begone, evil spirit!
Begone, evil spirit!

18:42.140 --> 18:48.730
Begone, evil spirit! Begone, evil spirit!
Begone, evil spirit!

18:43.870 --> 18:45.160
So noisy...

18:45.830 --> 18:48.730
Shoot, I fell asleep. What time is it?

18:48.730 --> 18:50.270
Ms. Alina! Ms. Alina!

18:50.270 --> 18:51.920
Look! Look! Look!

18:51.920 --> 18:53.610
Someone broke in?

18:53.610 --> 18:55.600
It's obviously a ghost!

19:01.840 --> 19:03.410
I get it.

19:03.410 --> 19:07.660
So even ghosts are trying to 
get in the way of my work now?

19:08.620 --> 19:10.780
If I were afraid of ghosts,

19:10.780 --> 19:14.600
how could I stay up all night working overtime?!

19:21.180 --> 19:22.130
Hmph.

19:22.130 --> 19:24.990
You hit it?! You exorcised a ghost by hitting it?!

19:25.690 --> 19:28.190
Wait, this is the guy from...

19:28.190 --> 19:31.520
Whatever he is, we should go get Mister Jade!

19:31.930 --> 19:34.670
I can't stay here any longer!

19:35.000 --> 19:36.820
Huh?

19:48.150 --> 19:49.410
Damn it.

19:55.860 --> 19:57.100
Jade...

19:59.070 --> 20:00.500
Don't die, okay?

20:07.370 --> 20:09.640
<i>I have to get stronger.</i>

20:11.170 --> 20:13.480
What are you doing lying around out here?

20:14.150 --> 20:15.230
Alina?!

20:15.230 --> 20:18.690
Mister Jade! A ghost! We saw a ghost!

20:18.920 --> 20:20.330
A ghost?

20:22.340 --> 20:25.980
It was probably the work of a Ghost monster.

20:25.980 --> 20:27.330
A Ghost?

20:27.330 --> 20:32.910
When Alina punched him, a white shadow 
flew out of him and disappeared, right?

20:32.910 --> 20:34.290
Yes, that's right.

20:34.590 --> 20:37.740
Only monsters die in that way.

20:37.740 --> 20:40.760
A Ghost must have possessed him at some point.

20:41.090 --> 20:42.280
Hear that?

20:42.280 --> 20:45.620
We know what the ghost was now.
Isn't that enough?

20:45.930 --> 20:47.550
But it's a monster!

20:47.550 --> 20:50.010
Isn't that scary?

20:52.400 --> 20:54.000
Did you see that?!

20:54.590 --> 20:55.710
See what?

20:55.710 --> 21:00.480
Why is it that the strong ones never 
see these things when it counts?!

21:00.920 --> 21:02.730
A b-b-black shadow...

21:03.160 --> 21:04.450
The reaper!

21:06.290 --> 21:07.410
Skill activate!

21:07.410 --> 21:09.410
<b>Sigurth Beast</b>

21:08.020 --> 21:09.410
Sigurth Beast!

21:10.810 --> 21:12.650
Yeah, someone's out there.

21:13.160 --> 21:14.100
After him!

21:14.890 --> 21:18.000
It could be someone dangerous. You wait here.

21:18.000 --> 21:18.680
Huh?

21:18.680 --> 21:21.170
Wait! Don't leave me!

21:21.570 --> 21:25.690
Don't leave me here all alone!

21:26.910 --> 21:28.050
Hold it!

21:31.510 --> 21:32.680
Damn!

21:46.970 --> 21:47.810
Bright!

21:49.350 --> 21:52.890
I'm sure he came this way, 
but I don't sense anything.

21:54.040 --> 21:56.200
Whoever it is, he sure runs fast.

22:05.960 --> 22:07.180
Who's there?

22:07.930 --> 22:10.550
I have waited for this day.

23:51.990 --> 24:00.250
<b>It May Be a Trap, but I Have to  Keep Moving Forward</b>

23:51.990 --> 24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

23:53.220 --> 23:54.130
Next time,

23:54.130 --> 23:58.150
"It May Be a Trap, but I Have 
to Keep Moving Forward."
